psion/chatter #1959, from hzk, 1173 chars, Mar 17 19:35 95
Comment to 1950.
----------
The way I use to detect a directory is as below:

        PROC isdir%:(f$)
                LOCAL fzts$(130),e%
                LOCAL ver%,attrib%,size&,mdate&,spare&
                fzts$=f$+chr$(0)
                e%=CALL($887,ADDR(fzts$)+1,ADDR(ver%),0,0,0)
                IF attrib% AND $10
                        RETURN 1
                ELSE
                        RETURN 0
                ENDIF 
        ENDP

Thus if you call:  
       
       ret%=isdir%:("LOC::M:\WRD")

ret% will be set to 1 if the \WRD directory exists on drive M.
As you can see from the variable names, this reads other file data
also.  A similar useful function is:

        PROC isit%:(f$)
                LOCAL h%
                IF IOOPEN(h%,f$,$30)
                        RETURN 0
                ELSE
                        IOCLOSE(h%)
                ENDIF
                RETURN 1
        ENDP

This can detect the existance of an SSD or Serial 3-Link.
Thus:
        
        ret%=isit%:("REM::C:\*.*")

will return 1 only if the Serial 3-Link is properly connected to
the Psion.

I suppose this really should be in psion/opl!

Roger.


